  "description": "Construction of a part two storey part single storey rear extension and a two storey side extension",
  "development_type": "Other house holder developments",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by reason of its design, bulk, mass, scale and siting, would overly dominate the side and rear of the host dwelling, would result in a detrimental loss of symmetry across the terrace row, would result in a loss of the open aspect between dwellings and would disrupt the planned layout of the Becontree Estate. It would thereby cause harm to the character and appearance of the area, including&nbsp;moderate&nbsp;harm to the non-designated heritage asset. The proposal would therefore be contrary to the following policies which seek to ensure that developments are sympathetic to local character and historic distinctiveness:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December, 2024)Policy HC1 of the London Plan (March 2021)The Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012)Policies SPP6, SP2, DMD1, DMD4&nbsp;and DMD5 of The Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September, 2024)"
  ],
